1. Slint
--------

The user interface is built with Slint (https://slint.dev), by SixtyFPS GmbH,
which is available under three licences:

    GPL-3.0-only
    OR LicenseRef-Slint-Royalty-free-2.0
    OR LicenseRef-Slint-Software-3.0

Facet uses Slint under the Royalty-free Desktop, Mobile, and Web Applications
License, version 2.0. That licence requires attribution, and clause 2 gives two
ways to provide it. Facet does the first:

    (a) Display the AboutSlint widget in an "About" screen or dialog that is
        accessible from the top level menu of the Application.

"About Facet" is therefore an item on the status item's menu, below the
separator beside Quit, and that menu is this app's top level menu: Facet is an accessory application and has no
application menu bar of its own. Choosing it opens the About screen directly,
with the AboutSlint widget on it.

Reaching About only by opening Settings and hunting for a tab would depend on
reading "accessible from" loosely, which is not a footing to put a licence
condition on. Three things therefore have to stay true together, and a build
that breaks any of them is out of compliance: the menu item exists, it opens the
About screen, and that screen shows the widget.

The same licence also forbids distributing Slint on its own without an
application around it, forbids use in an embedded system, and forbids shipping
an application that exposes Slint's own APIs. None of those is a constraint
Facet comes near, and all three are recorded so that a future change does not
walk into one.

The full text of all three Slint licences ships inside the slint crate, under
LICENSES/ in its source.


